# Balance counts only the players still in the game (CR 800.4a): one who has left has no lands and no cards in hand, and
# counted, would make the fewest zero. Bot2's library holds just its opening seven, so it loses by drawing from an empty
# library on turn 2 (CR 704.5b), and turns go Bot3, Bot1. On turn 6 Bot1 (three Plains, six cards in hand once Balance
# is cast) casts Balance against Bot3 (two Forests, seven cards): Bot1 keeps two Plains and sacrifices the third, and Bot3 discards one card,
# down to two lands and six cards each. Nobody has a creature.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Plains
Plains
Balance
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x7

[Bot3 Deck]
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot3.Main1]
Bot3.Hand.Forest.Play
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T5 Bot3.Main1]
Bot3.Hand.Forest.Play
[T6 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Balance.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Plains; Plains)
Bot3.Choose(Forest)

[Expect]
Turn = 6
Bot2.Status = Lost
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
Bot1.Hand.Count = 6
Bot3.Battlefield.Count = 2
Bot3.Hand.Count = 6
